  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Currently in the Open Beta, even when you are actively using a controller, the hand-tracking grip position & rotation always takes precedent. This is less than ideal for when you're in a game world or just trying to navigate the menus quickly. And for systems with poor hand-tracking quality or where the aim pose for the controllers don't match the aim pose for the hands, this can make the menus incredibly difficult to use. \n\nThere need to be an option to allow hand tracking to only affect the current gesture being made and the fingers of the avatar (which is different from the other request for an option to completely disable hand tracking). When the option is on, the wrist, grip, and aim poses from the controllers should be used when at all times unless the controllers are not being tracked.\n\nEdit: Apparently, the original reason I though we'd need this, might be bugs in Virtual Desktop and OpenComposite.\n\nHere are some other open issues that might be the same problem:\n\nhttps://feedback.vrchat.com/open-beta/p/1480-option-to-revert-controller-pointer-back-to-how-it-was\n\nhttps://feedback.vrchat.com/open-beta/p/1481-avatar-hands-are-static-when-switching-from-hand-tracking-to-controllers-vi\n\nhttps://feedback.vrchat.com/open-beta/p/1480-unable-to-switch-between-using-controllers-and-hand-tracking-forced-to-use",
